# Corpus fixtures encode line endings ON PURPOSE.
#
# reliability-corpus/known-good/modern-node-idioms/.env.example is CRLF because
# that is the shape that triggered KI #49 (env-integrity split on a bare \n,
# leaving a trailing \r on every line, which the trailing-whitespace rule then
# matched — 123 of 123 checks were false positives). If git normalises it to LF
# on checkout, the guard still passes but tests nothing at all.
#
# -text disables all EOL conversion so the bytes on disk are the bytes in git.
reliability-corpus/**/.env.example -text
